 "title": "Rhodosporidium toruloides Metabolic Network",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around Rhodosporidium toruloides, an organism with various metabolic connections. It has a genome assembly linked to BOT-A2, which contains the GFP gene. R. toruloides is exposed to nitrogen starvation and has a lipidomic analysis linked to IFO0880. It also has a metabolism that produces acetate and has proteins like NP11 and PDC1. Additionally, it has various chemical compounds like linoleic acid, oleic acid, and stearic acid. The cluster also includes other organisms like S. cerevisiae, which has a high expression level of PDC1 and uses NADH. The TCA cycle and EPS method are also mentioned in the cluster.",
